---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Circle from '../components/Circle.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="SECURITY" description="How to report a security issue in Original.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title"><Circle /> SECURITY</h1>
    <p class="lede">Reporting, scope, and the limits of a static site. Last updated 2026-11-04.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose legal-prose">
    <p>
      Original is a static site served by GitHub Pages. There is no login, no database, no write
      API, and no server-side application code. The main security surface is the published
      content, the client-side tools, and the links between them.
    </p>

    <h2>REPORTING</h2>
    <p>
      Send reports to <a href="mailto:security@original.wales">security@original.wales</a>.
      The machine-readable contact is in
      <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a> (RFC 9116).
    </p>
    <p>
      Please include the URL, a description of the issue, reproduction steps, and any relevant
      browser or platform details. Do not open a public issue for a vulnerability.
    </p>

    <h2>SCOPE</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Content or files that could mislead users or distribute malware.</li>
      <li>Cross-site scripting or injection in the site's own pages and tools.</li>
      <li>Broken access controls or exposed secrets in the public repository.</li>
      <li>Dependency vulnerabilities that affect the built site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Out of scope: denial-of-service testing, social engineering, physical attacks, and testing
      third-party services linked from the site. Do not access data that is not yours, disrupt the
      site, or attempt to bypass GitHub's platform controls.
    </p>

    <h2>GOOD-FAITH RESEARCH</h2>
    <p>
      Good-faith research that respects this scope is welcome. There is no bug bounty. Reports are
      read and answered when they are specific and reproducible. This page is not a legal
      safe-harbor statement and does not authorize activity that would otherwise be unlawful.
    </p>

    <h2>DEPENDENCIES</h2>
    <p>
      The site is built with Astro and deployed through GitHub Actions. Dependency and platform
      issues should be reported to the relevant upstream project as well as to this site if the
      published output is affected.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
